2. Ventricular thrombosis diagnosed by echocardiography and/or cardiac magnetic resonance;
3. Acute ST-segment-elevation myocardial infarction within 60 days;
4. Cardiac surgery within 60 days;
5. Unstable angina;
6. Pregnancy.

